/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - The half-bridge has two switches, S1 on top and S2 below, in series across the DC bus Vdc.
   - With S1 on, vAO = +Vdc/2; with S2 on, vAO = −Vdc/2.
   - vo = Σ (2Vdc/nπ) sin nωt, n = 1, 3, 5, … ω = 2πf is the output angular frequency and n the harmonic order.
   - The capacitors must be large enough that O does not move while they carry the load current.
   - The full bridge has two legs: S1 over S2 (leg A) and S3 over S4 (leg B), with the load between the midpoints A and B.
   - vo = Σ (4Vdc/nπ) sin nωt, n = 1, 3, 5, … The fundamental peak is 4Vdc/π = 1.273Vdc (rms 0.9Vdc); the nth harmonic is 1/n of it.
   - Even harmonics and DC are absent because the wave has half-wave symmetry, v(t + T/2) = −v(t).
   - With an R-L load the current cannot reverse at the instant the voltage does.
   - Imax = (Vdc/R)·tanh(T/4τ) T is the output period in seconds and τ = L/R in seconds.
   - Follow one half cycle.
*/
