/* book Worked example 2: Q: A full bridge with Vdc = 220 V feeds R = 10 Ω in series with L = 25 mH at 50 Hz in square-wave mode. Find (a) the peak load current, (b) how long the feedback diodes conduct after each switching, (c) the rms current from the first four harmonics and (d) the power and average supply current.
   1. τ = L/R = 0.025/10 = 2.5 ms and T = 1/50 = 20 ms, so T/4τ = 20/10 = 2.
   2. (a) Imax = (Vdc/R) tanh(T/4τ) = (220/10) × tanh 2 = 22 × 0.9640 = 21.21 A.
   3. (b) tx = τ ln(1 + tanh(T/4τ)) = 2.5 ms × ln 1.9640 = 2.5 × 0.6750 = 1.69 ms.
   4. (c) ωL = 2π × 50 × 0.025 = 7.854 Ω; Vn = 4Vdc/(nπ√2) and In = Vn/√(R² + (nωL)²):
   5. n = 1: V1 = 198.07 V, |Z1| = 12.72 Ω, I1 = 15.577 A.
   6. n = 3: V3 = 66.02 V, |Z3| = 25.60 Ω, I3 = 2.579 A.
   7. n = 5: V5 = 39.61 V, |Z5| = 40.52 Ω, I5 = 0.978 A.
   8. n = 7: V7 = 28.30 V, |Z7| = 55.88 Ω, I7 = 0.506 A.
   9. Irms ≈ √(15.577² + 2.579² + 0.978² + 0.506²) = 15.83 A. Integrating the exponential current itself gives 15.83 A.
   10. (d) Only R takes power: P = Irms² R = 15.83² × 10 = 2507 W. The average supply current is P/Vdc = 2507/220 = 11.40 A.
   Answer: Imax = 21.21 A; the feedback diodes conduct for 1.69 ms after each switching; Irms ≈ 15.83 A; P ≈ 2507 W and the average supply current is 11.40 A. */
