/* book Worked example: Q: A full bridge has Vdc = 200 V and a 50 Hz output. (a) With single-pulse modulation and d = 30° (a 60° pulse), find the fundamental peak, the rms output and the 3rd harmonic. (b) It is changed to 4 equal pulses per half cycle, each 10° wide. Find the modulation index, the carrier frequency, the rms output, the fundamental and the strongest harmonics.
   1. (a) 4Vdc/π = 4 × 200/π = 254.65 V. b1 = 254.65 × sin 30° = 254.65 × 0.5 = 127.3 V peak.
   2. Vrms = 200√(60/180) = 200 × 0.5774 = 115.5 V.
   3. b3 = (254.65/3) × sin 90° = 84.9 V peak, which is 67 % of the fundamental.
   4. (b) Each pulse can be at most 180°/4 = 45° wide, so M = 10/45 = 0.222; the carrier runs at 2pf = 2 × 4 × 50 = 400 Hz.
   5. Total on-time per half cycle = 4 × 10° = 40°, so Vrms = 200√(40/180) = 94.3 V.
   6. Pulse centres 22.5°, 67.5°, 112.5°, 157.5°: Σ sin γk = 2(sin 22.5° + sin 67.5°) = 2(0.3827 + 0.9239) = 2.6131, so b1 = 254.65 × sin 5° × 2.6131 = 254.65 × 0.0872 × 2.6131 = 58.0 V peak.
   7. The same formula gives b3 = 23.8 V, b5 = 23.3 V, b7 = 54.5 V and b9 = 52.3 V: the strongest harmonics are the 7th and 9th (2p ∓ 1), at 94 % and 90 % of the fundamental.
   Answer: (a) 127.3 V fundamental peak, 115.5 V rms, 3rd harmonic 84.9 V. (b) M = 0.222, fc = 400 Hz, Vrms = 94.3 V, fundamental 58.0 V peak, strongest harmonics the 7th and 9th. */
