/* book Worked example 2: Q: A single-pulse full bridge with Vdc = 220 V must give a fundamental of 150 V rms. Find the pulse width, the rms output and the THD.
   1. b1 = 150 × √2 = 212.1 V and 4Vdc/π = 280.1 V, so sin d = 212.1/280.1 = 0.7573.
   2. d = sin⁻¹ 0.7573 = 49.23°, so the pulse is 2d = 98.5° wide.
   3. Vrms = 220√(98.5/180) = 220 × 0.7396 = 162.7 V.
   4. THD = √(Vrms² − V1²)/V1 = √(162.7² − 150²)/150 = 63.0/150 = 42.0 %.
   5. Check one harmonic: b3 = (4 × 220/3π) sin(3 × 49.23°), which is 35.3 V rms, 23.5 % of the fundamental.
   Answer: 2d = 98.5°, Vrms = 162.7 V and THD = 42.0 %. */
